On the scheduled day, a trained inspector arrives at your Bangalore address. They conduct a visual inspection, photograph the car from all angles, and note any existing scratches or dents on a digital checklist. The inspector also verifies ownership documents (RC, insurance, PUC) and uploads the inspection report instantly to the tracking portal, so you can view it live.

**4. Secure Loading onto the Carrier**  
After inspection, the car is driven onto a low‑loader or enclosed container, depending on the service you chose. Professional handlers use wheel‑chocks, straps, and anti‑scratch pads to prevent movement or damage during transit. A short video of the loading process is automatically attached to your tracking page, giving you visual confirmation.

**5. Transit – Real‑Time GPS Monitoring**  
The carrier is equipped with a GPS tracker linked to the company’s central operations center. As the vehicle travels the 350 km stretch via NH 48, the map on your dashboard updates every few seconds, showing current location, speed, and estimated time of arrival (ETA). You also receive automated SMS alerts at key milestones: departure from Bangalore, entry into Karnataka‑Tamil Nadu border, and arrival at the Chennai depot.

**6. Arrival & Pre‑Delivery Inspection in Chennai**  
Upon reaching Chennai, the car is unloaded onto a pre‑designated spot. A second inspector repeats the documentation process, comparing the post‑transit photos with the pre‑loading ones. Any discrepancies are flagged instantly on the tracking portal.

**7. Hando‑Over & Final Confirmation**  
You (or your authorized representative) meet the driver, sign the delivery receipt, and receive the original inspection report. The tracking system automatically marks the job as **“Completed – Bangalore to Chennai car relocation.”** A post‑relocation survey is sent to gather feedback.

**8. Post‑Delivery Support**  
For the next 30 days, the company offers a warranty on transit‑related damages. All records—including the real‑time tracking log—are stored in your account for future reference.

