      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Doorstep Vehicle Inspection &amp; Pre‑Transit Condition Reporting</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;">**Doorstep Vehicle Inspection Protocol**

Before any long‑haul move, the vehicle that will carry your belongings must undergo a meticulous doorstep inspection. This protocol ensures that the transport process begins with a vehicle in optimal condition, protecting both cargo and driver.

1. **Pre‑Transit Condition Assessment**  
   • *Exterior & Body*: Inspect for dents, scratches, rust, and existing damage. Verify that all doors, windows, and seals close securely.  
   • *Interior & Cargo Space*: Check the condition of seats, flooring, and storage compartments. Ensure there are no leaks or loose fixtures that could shift during transit.  
   • *Mechanical & Safety Systems*: Confirm that brakes, lights, horn, and turn signals function correctly. Test tire pressure, tread depth, and spare tire integrity.  
   • *Fluid Levels & Battery*: Verify engine oil, coolant, brake fluid, and windshield washer levels. Inspect the battery for corrosion and charge status.  
   This assessment is recorded in a digital log that assigns a unique inspection ID to each vehicle.

2. **Photographic Evidence**  
   High‑resolution images are taken from multiple angles—front, rear, sides, and interior—capturing any pre‑existing marks or damages. Each photo is timestamped and geo‑tagged, then uploaded to a secure cloud folder linked to the vehicle’s inspection ID. This visual audit serves as a reference point for any future disputes and reassures clients that their vehicle’s condition is documented before departure.

3. **Handover Checklist**  
   When the vehicle is handed over to the logistics team, the following items are verified and signed off:  
   • Inspection report and photographic archive.  
   • Driver’s license, registration, and insurance documents.  
   • Route plan and GPS device configuration.  
   • Emergency kit, spare parts, and loading tools.  
   A signed “Vehicle Handover Form” confirms that the driver accepts responsibility for any damage that may arise after the inspection. The form is signed by both the vehicle owner and the logistics representative, ensuring clear accountability.

By integrating this protocol, our packers and movers bangalore to chennai service guarantees that every vehicle is road‑ready, well‑documented, and legally compliant. This proactive approach minimizes the risk of damage claims, speeds up customs clearance, and provides peace of mind to clients embarking on long‑distance relocations.</div>
